From: FatBoy721 <203330788+FatBoy721@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:36:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g17: add the J714s GPU bins of a third unit (FatBoy721)

GPU voltage bins are fused per chip, and this J714s's differ from both
units already carried (betizzel's J714S, TripleU613's J714S_TRIPLEU) in
almost every active state. Add its tables as J714S_FATBOY721, selected
only by the "apple,j714s-gpu-fatboy721" GPU compatible, exactly as the
TripleU613 unit is (G17J714s probe, so the fuse-mask guard applies).

The tables come from that Mac's own ADT, read in macOS 27.3 beta 1
(26C5035r) with `ioreg -l -w0 -p IODeviceTree -r -n sgx` and the
afr-perf-states / cs-perf-states nodes:
- perf-states holds table 0 then table 1 (= perf-states1); the SRAM
  tables likewise. 14 states, 0..1620 MHz, top state 1045/1025 mV.
- afr-perf-states == cs-perf-states (u64 uV/Hz, min SRAM 775000 uV);
  auxiliary SRAM = max(775 mV, core), as for the other units.

Tested on that unit (stub mBoot-20457.60.65.0.1, DCP at 120 Hz):
"GPU firmware build: 26C5035r for T6050 G17S", both initdata
acknowledged, [drm] Initialized aurora, renderD128. Hyprland renders on
it (CDRMRenderer card0, scanout on apple-drm): es2gears 118.5-119.2 FPS
(78 on llvmpipe), Hyprland ~4% CPU (was ~1260%), ~12-13 W on battery
(was ~30 W), no GPU errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
  drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/driver.rs             |  4 +++
  drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g17/fw/m5/initdata.rs | 51 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
  drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/hw/t6050.rs           |  6 ++++
  3 files changed, 61 insertions(+)

